  "body": "**Blocked by:** #93\n\n## Context\n\nBackground consumers must not mark mail read as an IMAP side effect, and real providers reject excessive concurrent connections.\n\n## Task\n\nUse `BODY.PEEK[]`, never `BODY[]`, whenever content is fetched without an explicit user mark-read action, including AI/background reads. Add a per-account IMAP concurrency limiter and provider-aware backoff for connection-limit responses such as Gmail's simultaneous-connection rejection. Retries must respect the persisted mail sync state and must not create parallel retry storms.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- Background PEEK semantics, per-account connection limits, and delayed backoff.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- Live IDLE/push synchronization, partial-fetch fallback, oversized attachments, and message-id conflict hardening, which remain in their existing issues.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Background body fetch leaves `\\\\Seen` unchanged.\n- An explicit mark-read path still maps to `\\\\Seen`.\n- Concurrent work for one account never exceeds its configured/provider limit.\n- A connection-limit response schedules delayed retry rather than immediate recursion.\n",
